        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without pneumonic infiltrates, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout the stay. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids for hydration support. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged in stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please ensure close follow-up and review of his long-term COPD management. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
